The ternary expressions evaluate to either `'active'` or `''`, and passing `''` to `classList.add()` or `classList.remove()` causes the crash.

The fix is:
```javascript
if(i===current){
  s.classList.add('active');
} else {
  s.classList.remove('active');
}
```

